Exponential UI, no new component), testId `testIds.tabs`, its options = `tabs` in order, each the label `copy.tabs[id]` followed by its `count` as a muted number when not null; on a phone it scrolls sideways when it overflows (never icon-only, never wrapping). TABS BY KIND (`kinds`): a chat, an agent and the Assistant = chat · issues · sessions · results; an app = chat · preview · data · versions · sessions · results. COUNTS (`count`, issues/sessions/results only; 0 = null): issues = every issue of the tree (session-chat.json's union, nested ones included), sessions = every session UNDER the root (its children and theirs; #EXP-1731's subagent children included; the root itself never), results = results-tab.json's results of the tree. GEAR (`gear`): agent, assistant and app; never a chat. It opens the kind's SETTINGS as an opened item (`open: settings`): an agent = THE agent settings page (agent-settings.json: prompt, triggers, defaults; the Assistant's = settings/assistant), an app = the app's settings page (apps.json Settings, the app's agent's prompt/triggers/defaults on the same page once apps.agent_id lands, #EXP-1730). BODIES: chat = the ROOT's OWN SESSION VIEW for EVERY kind (owner 2026-11-08): its raw work (THE ONE transcript of #EXP-1736 transcript-grouping.json: MessageBubble + avatar + name, the tool/thought/subagent `trace` rows under the agent's bubble) with its own message cards inline, THE Dock and THE composer (the view NEW-46 showed on a single-session chat, now always; the old dispatcher Conversation without the root's work is gone; no second message view anywhere); no session's work is visible nowhere: the root's = Chat, every descendant's = its Sessions row, a single-session chat's Sessions tab is empty (never a row for the root itself); plans and questions stay INLINE in it (and in Needs you); a plan row opens the plan page (plan-page.json) as an opened item. issues = the tree's issues as THE issue rows (status glyph, mono identifier, title; nested ones indented under their parent), led by the `+` icon button (THE Menu: Link an issue > THE search list, New issue); a row opens that issue IN PLACE (`open: issue`, the embedded issue body of session-chat.json EXP-1316). sessions = THE tree rows of every session under the root (SessionRow small + TreeGuides, markState, subagents included as child rows); a row opens that session IN PLACE (`open: session`, the raw work + its composer). results = results-tab.json's body. preview / data / versions = apps.json's Preview, Data (app-records.json `dataTab`) and Versions bodies. An OPENED item (issue, session, plan, settings) carries THE back link (the existing back link row: the `ui-back` glyph + its label; phones: the pushed page's `‹` header) to the tab it came from (settings and a plan: back to where they were opened). LAYOUT (`sessionScreen`, every mirror replays `cases` comparing the WHOLE value): WIDE (web ≥ `beside.breakpoint` px and the IDE) = the beside rule: whenever the active tab is not chat OR an item is opened, the body = TWO panes, the chat pane (`beside.chat` fr, min `beside.chatMinWidth` px, THE same chat body with its composer) : the tab pane (`beside.pane` fr, the active tab's body, or the opened item over it), a hairline between (`layout: beside`, testId `testIds.beside`); the Chat tab alone = the chat full width (`layout: chat`). NARROW (phones, web < breakpoint) = ONE pane: `chat`, the tab's body (`tab`) or the opened item (`item`, a pushed page over the tab). ACTIVE = the requested tab when it is one of the kind's tabs (legacy `?tab=` values map through `legacyTabs` first), else the kind's default: an app `preview` when wide (apps.json), else `chat`. OPEN (`open` in: issue | session | plan | settings, anything else = null): a requested `settings` (the retired app `?tab=settings`) opens settings when nothing else is open; settings only with `gear` (else null). ALGORITHM: k = `kinds[kind]` (unknown = session); tabs = k.tabs as {id, label, count}; req = `legacyTabs[requested]` ?? requested; active = req when in k.tabs, else (wide ? k.wideDefault : `chat`); layout = wide ? (active ≠ chat or open ? `beside` : `chat`) : (open ? `item` : active = chat ? `chat` : `tab`). Mirrors: TS src/session-screen.ts, desktop `domain::session_screen`, iOS ExpCore `SessionScreen.swift`, Android `domain/SessionScreen.kt`. STATUS WORD (owner 2026-11-09, one rule ×4, `sessionScreenStatus`, every mirror replays `statusCases`): the subtitle's `status` = THE TREE's word, lowercase `copy.status`: `needsInput` while any non-ended session of the tree needs input, else `working` while any non-ended one is busy, else `queued` while the root is queued, else `done` once the root ended, else `idle` (an empty tree = `idle`); it is never dropped. An app's subtitle = this word · apps.json `editorHeader`'s DEVICE part (the device's name, else `copy.noDeviceOnline`) and that function's TONE; a chat's and an agent's device = the root's device name. ACTIVE FOLLOWS THE OPENED ITEM: `open` session = the `sessions` tab active, `open` issue = `issues`, when the kind has that tab (a plan and settings keep the active tab). TAB SIZING ×4: every segment is sized to its label (+ count), never stretched to equal widths and never squeezed; the strip scrolls sideways when it overflows. APP LEAD ×4: the app's BoardGlyph sits IN the lead disc (the chat header's `disc` on the muted fill), never bare, the version pill right after the name. PHONE ITEM ×4 (web-mobile too): an opened item is a pushed page: its own header (‹ back + the item's title) replaces the screen header AND the tabs. TONE ×4: the subtitle wears editorHeader's tones: `attention` (the needs-input amber) while the word is needsInput (an app also while its device part is `copy.noDeviceOnline`), `active` while working or queued, else `muted`.",
